id: pm-rust-bounded-read-sessions
title: Stream certified native reads under caller resource limits
description: "Embeddable bounded read sessions for non-Node hosts, reusing existing native query and output contracts."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: embedding,"gh:unbraind/pm-rust#110",resources,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-23T14:33:11.991Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T23:14:02.408Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-24T21:48:10.270Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-23T22:54:51.000Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Large synthetic trackers respect a declared memory ceiling; cancellation releases resources; wire results remain oracle-conformant; compact JSON/TOON, typed refusals and remedies, README and example; read-only non-git public-tracker validation; unchanged CI gates."
parent: pm-rust-u4al
resolution: "Certified streaming reads honor caller memory/cancellation limits while retaining oracle wire contracts, actionable compact outputs and measured non-git public-tracker evidence."
expected_result: "Large synthetic trackers respect a declared memory ceiling; cancellation releases resources; wire results remain oracle-conformant; compact JSON/TOON, typed refusals and remedies, README and example; read-only non-git public-tracker validation; unchanged CI gates."
actual_result: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/110, merged 2026-10-23T22:54:51Z, merge ec39af2b06d3884c466b5770b41e1cdb745f1cd6: Certified streaming reads honor caller memory/cancellation limits while retaining oracle wire contracts, actionable compact outputs and measured non-git public-tracker evidence."
comments[30]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T14:33:35.077Z",codex-agent,"Overlap audit: core SDK listAllComplete/certifyCompleteListResult own completeness and CLI list owns pagination. pm-context owns durable context packs and usage receipts; pm-web consumes complete SDK lists. Native pagination is pm-rust-ufzy and latency is pm-rust-wdj4. No existing embedding resource contract found. Reuse Workspace::list_page, strict decoding, lifecycle registries and JSON/TOON codecs. Add bounded private snapshot admission, cooperative cancellation and certified session receipts without another core query or parity pin. The crate remains native Rust; typed TypeScript is used for the validation harness."
  "2026-10-23T14:44:13.698Z",codex-agent,"Implementation decision: immutable private disk snapshots isolate admitted reads from later writers while preserving original cursor identity. Admission accounts native working-set reserve and bounds every source read; the declared ledger ceiling is distinct from measured process RSS. Reuse canonical list_page, strict complete-item decoder and duplicate checks. Pull ownership supplies backpressure, cancellation is cooperative between copying/query boundaries, and completion/failure/cancel/drop remove snapshots. Add unchanged npm/Bun aliases for the existing Rust release gate and a Bun CI aggregate. Local work is restricted to targeted tests, lint/typecheck and focused validation because the host is saturated."
  "2026-10-23T15:04:31.443Z",codex-agent,Initial CI and targeted regression found that the canonical output renderer returns an omission-only receipt for infeasible budgets rather than always raising an error. The embedding wrapper now refuses result_omitted before it can mark a session complete and cleans up the snapshot. Keep the canonical renderer unchanged. Also isolate fixture init with an explicit tracker path so linked-test sandbox environment cannot redirect initialization. CI aggregate thresholds remain unchanged.
  "2026-10-23T15:13:48.701Z",codex-agent,"Focused linked suites passed 7 SDK and 4 CLI regressions before the strengthened complete-source-deletion check. Public-oracle validation distinguishes SDK convenience envelopes from CLI envelopes: use the real SDK complete-list certificate and row comparisons, plus the existing published CLI launcher under a fixed clock for byte-exact page comparisons. Frozen sessions now load lifecycle registries from snapshot storage while retaining only cursor identity from the original tracker. Behavioral reverts are being verified independently; no release thresholds or oracle pins changed."
  "2026-10-23T15:20:20.151Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof complete: separately disable Admission::charge, bypass Workspace::with_read_snapshot, restore lifecycle reads to the live query root, bypass cleanup on cancellation, and remove the result_omitted guard. Each isolated variant compiled and failed its targeted regression (five expected exit-101 test failures); all original functions were restored. Restored linked suites passed 7 SDK plus 4 CLI tests; the npm/Bun aggregate wiring regression passed 1 test; formatting, strict Clippy, private rustdoc and strict erasable TypeScript checks passed. The public copy has 78 items and unchanged authoritative source hashes. Final large measurements and CI remain pending."
  "2026-10-23T15:41:49.605Z",codex-agent,"Final resource and oracle evidence: 10,000 SDK-generated items in 10 pages, 1,959,611 source bytes, admission 381,185,760 bytes, peak RSS 43,688 KiB, native wall 28,001 ms, output 988,986 bytes; public tracker copy at 5862034 has 78 items in 1 page, 757,075 source bytes, admission 131,681,424 bytes, peak RSS 13,440 KiB, wall 437 ms, output 12,549 bytes. Both used a 536,870,912-byte declared ceiling and passed complete-list certificates and identity equality. All 11 pages matched canonical CLI JSON payloads with indentation normalization only; source hashes were unchanged. Binary SHA-256 was stable before and after validation. Seven behavioral reverts failed independently, including clock charging and duplicate-path remedies; all restored. CLI 2026.10.23 overlap rechecked; package oracle remains pinned to 2026.10.21. Evidence and reproduction: docs/BOUNDED_READ_SESSIONS.md. PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/110. Full CI aggregate evidence pending; item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-23T15:43:20.715Z",codex-agent,"Final focused validation: pm test --run --progress --timeout 900 passed all 3 linked commands, totaling 9 SDK session tests, 4 CLI session tests and 1 npm/Bun aggregate wiring test; zero failed or ignored. Strict Clippy across all targets/features, formatting, private rustdoc and strict erasable TypeScript checks passed. Real storage loss and explicit CLI clock selection are covered. Core decode_unique supplies both duplicate-file paths. Clock-storage reservation has its own failing behavioral revert. All seven revert proofs restored; no generated data or binaries are tracked. Implementation is ready for CI and review in PR 110; only full CI evidence remains pending. Release claim without closing so the orchestrator can verify and close."
  "2026-10-23T15:52:07.547Z",codex-agent,"Exact-head Windows CI found a registry diagnostic path regression: normal reads reported canonical extended-length paths instead of the published caller spelling. Preserve query-root spelling for ordinary registry reads, while sessions resolve registry storage to their private snapshot. Existing workflow_fallbacks_and_settings_errors regression detected this. Reclaim for the compatibility correction; thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-23T15:56:21.378Z",codex-agent,"Windows diagnostic correction passes the targeted registry regression plus the 9 SDK, 4 CLI and 1 pipeline wiring tests locally. Repeated final-binary validation after the correction: synthetic 10,000 items / 10 pages, admission 381,185,760 bytes, peak RSS 43,396 KiB, wall 23,797 ms, output 988,986 bytes; public copy 78 items / 1 page, admission 131,681,424 bytes, peak RSS 13,568 KiB, wall 167 ms, output 12,549 bytes. Both remain under the declared 536,870,912-byte ceiling, with all 11 canonical oracle payload comparisons, SDK certificates, identity equality and unchanged source hashes passing. Final binary SHA-256 verified before/after: 6d591b2a41c1edc0c02fb2f055f2fc0f35cc333eb8acdcee9447ac1c13c3d35a. docs/BOUNDED_READ_SESSIONS.md updated. Release claim; Windows and full CI gates must verify the new head."
  "2026-10-23T16:33:37.805Z",codex-agent,"CI run 39982597630 completed the regular and coverage-instrumented suites, then enforced unchanged thresholds and found one uncovered output-cursor branch, two lines and 30 error-propagation regions. Add actual filesystem fault coverage, bounded-reader I/O tests and consumer-disconnect writer tests without SDK mocks. Coverage review also identified a delivery invariant: completion/pages must update only after successful terminal cleanup, so a cleanup error cannot certify an undelivered final page. Reclaim for that correction and complete fault-path verification; keep all four coverage thresholds at 100."
  "2026-10-23T17:07:49.714Z",codex-agent,"CI retained all four 100-percent thresholds and exposed untested storage propagation plus a final-cleanup ordering defect. Final-page cleanup now precedes receipt certification; failed cleanup remains terminal without counting an undelivered page. Added genuine output-cursor continuation over 300 rows, directory/read/write/flush faults, and consumer-disconnect coverage. All five linked commands passed: 14 SDK, 5 CLI, 1 framing, 1 pipeline and 1 registry regression tests, zero failures or ignored tests. Strict Clippy passed. Delivery-cleanup and output-cursor behavioral reverts compiled and each failed their new regression; restored code passed, bringing independent revert proofs to nine. Full npm and Bun release gates remain reserved for CI."
  "2026-10-23T17:14:54.325Z",codex-agent,"Final corrected-binary validation passed on SDK-created and read-only non-git public tracker copies. Synthetic: 10000 items, 10 pages, 1959611 source bytes, 381185760 admitted bytes, 43652 KiB peak RSS, 131120 ms wall, 988986 output bytes. Public copy: 78 items, 1 page, 757075 source bytes, 131681424 admitted bytes, 13824 KiB peak RSS, 782 ms wall, 12549 output bytes. Declared ceiling 536870912 bytes. Both complete SDK certificates passed; all identities and 11 canonical CLI JSON payloads matched after indentation normalization only. Source fingerprints unchanged. Measured binary SHA-256 b521fc24870ac80b095e3f417af765e58c0a50a616b455b04b8b0c7e430bfa71 matched before and after. Runnable Rust example completed 78 items in four pages with neither Node nor Git on PATH. Private rustdoc, formatting and strict Clippy passed. Runtime test-result recording is disabled by existing project policy; linked execution and this comment retain the results. Ready PR 110 remains subject to the unchanged full CI gates; claim released for orchestrator verification, item remains in progress."
  "2026-10-23T17:42:43.290Z",codex-agent,"The Windows aggregate completed both 603-test passes with zero failures or ignored tests. Lines, functions and branches reached 100 percent; one region remained uncovered in the instrumented SDK variant of actual temporary-directory creation failure. Existing CLI coverage exercised the production variant, but cfg(test) lifecycle hooks produce a distinct instrumented variant. Adding an isolated unit-process regression that invokes the real SDK against an actual blocked scratch parent, without changing production behavior or thresholds. Linux and macOS regular suites passed 620 and 609 tests respectively; all three latency guards and CodeQL passed."
  "2026-10-23T17:44:50.648Z",codex-agent,"Fresh-process SDK regression passed against a real file blocking the scratch directory; no environment mutation, SDK mock, production change or threshold reduction. The linked SDK suite now passes 15 tests, zero failures/ignored tests; the other four unchanged linked commands passed previously, for 23 focused tests. Strict Clippy and formatting passed. Production binary SHA-256 remains b521fc24870ac80b095e3f417af765e58c0a50a616b455b04b8b0c7e430bfa71, so the final 10000-item and public-copy measurements remain exact. Bun independently completed two 620-test passes and reached the same sole uncovered creation-error region, confirming the targeted cause. Ready PR 110 will carry the final exact-head full gate URL and counts. Item remains in progress, released for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-23T18:26:37.115Z",codex-agent,"Blocking review found that Path::exists suppressed schema lookup failures and allowed a session to certify defaults when the canonical list reader refused. Pulled the PR branch, merged advanced main and regenerated/checked the changelog inside the merge. Reusing this feature item for the correction: optional schema lookup will fall back only for NotFound, preserve canonical I/O path and error kind for other failures, and refuse admission before completion. Add a regular-file schema-parent regression and verify behavioral revert failure, targeted Rust tests, strict Clippy, and the unchanged npm/Bun CI aggregates."
  "2026-10-23T18:34:00.980Z",codex-agent,"Fixed blocking schema lookup refusal by replacing the lossy existence check with symlink_metadata and an explicit NotFound-only default branch. All other lookup errors retain the canonical read-path spelling and original OS error in PmRustError::Io, refusing admission before any certificate. Regression schema_parent_file_preserves_canonical_lookup_error compares path, NotADirectory kind and raw OS code with list_page for default/configured statuses and configured workflows. CLI regression schema_parent_file_never_certifies_cli_completion verifies JSON/TOON refusal, empty stdout, unchanged source and removed private scratch storage. Behavioral revert proof: restoring only the original Workspace::read_session made the SDK regression compile and fail with exit 101, reporting that schema lookup must refuse before session certification. Restored fix passed all 16 SDK and 6 CLI session tests, also through both matching pm-linked commands; strict all-target/all-feature Clippy and formatting passed. Ten independent behavioral revert proofs now exist. Prior resource measurements are retained as explicitly identified pre-review observations; completed large-fixture work was not repeated. Read-only health found no pending merge receipt; existing local environment advisories were left untouched, with the clean CI gate required for full health evidence."
  "2026-10-23T19:04:00.858Z",codex-agent,"Review round: remote head pulled and already contains main. GraphQL reports zero review threads and no CodeRabbit review body. Failed CI run 40004446634 shows Windows canonical list treats a schema parent file as NotFound, while the regression incorrectly requires Unix NotADirectory. Preserve strict Unix refusal assertions and verify Windows canonical fallback parity explicitly. Recheck the blocking lookup fix with an independent behavioral revert, self-review the complete diff, and run the unchanged native release gate."
  "2026-10-23T19:06:26.096Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof repeated at this head: replacing only the optional registry lookup in Workspace::read_session with the previous exists() check compiled successfully and failed both cargo +1.90.0 test --locked --lib read_session::tests::schema_parent_file_preserves_canonical_lookup_error -- --exact and cargo +1.90.0 test --locked --test read_session_contract schema_parent_file_never_certifies_cli_completion -- --exact, each exit 101. SDK reported admission unexpectedly succeeded; CLI returned exit 0 instead of 2. Restored the exact production source. Focused restored suites pass 16 SDK and 6 CLI tests on Unix. The added Windows regressions check canonical default-registry parity and cleanup rather than requiring a Unix-only OS error. Whole-diff self-review covered schema path components, bounded source errors, snapshot isolation, completion/cleanup, output continuations, and CLI writer failures; no additional instance of the swallowed lookup defect was found."
  "2026-10-23T19:10:58.495Z",codex-agent,"Coverage self-review: the non-NotFound registry error must also be exercised on Windows, where the file-parent case is NotFound. Added a platform-independent real invalid-filename regression for statuses and workflows using a NUL path from settings; it compares the exact canonical InvalidInput refusal and rejects admission. This preserves error-branch coverage on every release platform without mocking filesystem behavior or lowering thresholds."
  "2026-10-23T19:26:31.374Z",codex-agent,"Portable refusal revert proof: restoring only the previous exists() lookup compiled and made schema_invalid_path_preserves_canonical_lookup_error fail with exit 101 for admission unexpectedly succeeding. Restoring the exact source passed the test. All five existing pm-linked commands passed on retry (17 SDK, 6 CLI and three supporting tests; 26 total). The first linked CLI attempt hit bundle_integrity_torn_install during the oracle reinstall and passed after installation completed. Strict Clippy, private rustdoc, formatting and isolated CI-style health passed. The local unchanged just release-check attempt was explicitly stopped under heavy host contention after 334 library, 35 CLI unit and branch-merge tests passed and while ownership differentials continued; this is incomplete gate evidence. Push the reviewed candidate and require all unchanged full CI aggregates, including Windows and Bun, before proceeding to PR 105. No CodeRabbit review body exists; its issue comment says automatic review was skipped. Full health history advisories remain tracked separately by pm-rust-b4yl."
  "2026-10-23T19:29:03.183Z",codex-agent,"Final review candidate adds portable SDK and CLI invalid-filename checks alongside strict Unix file-parent refusals and explicit Windows canonical-default checks. Both portable regressions independently compiled and failed with only the old exists() behavior restored (exit 101): SDK admitted an invalid path; CLI leaked the private snapshot diagnostic instead of the canonical source diagnostic. All production bytes are restored. Final pm-linked CLI suite passed 7 tests; unchanged linked SDK/supporting suites passed 17 plus 3 tests, for 27 focused cases. Strict Clippy was corrected to use explicit ItemFilter/ListOptions defaults and rerun at unchanged warning policy. Final full gates are delegated to the unchanged CI matrix after push; local full gate was stopped as documented, never reported as passed. Release the claim for independent verification; keep the item in progress."
  "2026-10-23T19:31:57.739Z",codex-agent,"CI run 40011795454 reached the Windows-only test declarations and Clippy correctly rejected two documentation references to NotFound without code formatting. Correct both docstrings using inline code formatting; no executable logic, test assertions or thresholds change. Linux Clippy cannot inspect cfg(windows) declarations, so exact-head Windows CI remains required. Read the completed Windows job log directly while the aggregate run was still active because gh run view --log-failed defers logs until run completion."
  "2026-10-23T21:18:51.831Z",codex-agent,"Review round: PR 110 has zero review threads and no CodeRabbit reviews. The latest owner review flags lossy snapshot filename hashing; verify and cover it while merging main crash-recovery behavior, then run the unchanged full release gate and CI. No thread replies or resolutions."
  "2026-10-23T21:19:47.193Z",codex-agent,"Only conflicted file: .github/workflows/ci.yml. Retained both Bun setup and Linux strace installation before the unchanged aggregate step. Main mutation crash recovery and its corpus merge intact. Valid owner-review finding: use lossless native OS-string bytes in the snapshot digest, with a real non-git regression for both invalid-UTF-8 item filenames and parent directory names. Self-review checked admission, schema paths, native hashing, cursor identity, lifecycle cleanup, CLI framing and validation harness; no other instance in the native certificate path."
  "2026-10-23T21:20:19.439Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: restoring only Admission::copy filename hashing to relative.to_string_lossy().as_bytes() compiled and caused snapshot_digest_preserves_non_utf8_filename_and_directory_bytes to fail its unique-digest assertion (1 failed, exit 101). Exact production bytes restored; fixed test passed before the revert. No unresolved thread IDs exist; the owner review is the only actionable review finding. Health has no merge_receipts_pending; pre-existing history/provenance advisories and host extension skew are outside this merge scope."
  "2026-10-23T21:20:53.174Z",codex-agent,"All six pm-linked commands passed: 18 session unit tests, 7 CLI/SDK contract tests, 1 release-entrypoint test, 1 registry test, 1 writer test and 1 focused digest rerun (29 executions, 28 distinct tests). Reverted hashing failed as expected; restored hashing passes. No tracked dist assets exist. CodeRabbit only posted an automatic-review-skipped issue comment, with no outside-diff findings."
  "2026-10-23T21:57:26.517Z",codex-agent,"Local full just release-check passed fmt, strict all-target Clippy, private rustdoc and preceding test suites, then failed only relationship_large_edge_limit_finishes_at_budget_floor: its five-second native child was killed (no exit code) under heavy host load while the oracle returned the expected budget refusal. Orientation suite: 31 passed, 1 deadline failure. Existing follow-up pm-rust-local-packet-deadline covers this condition; no threshold or unrelated code changes. Retry that exact case in isolation and require all full CI aggregates on the pushed merge. Standalone just crash-check passed typechecking, ESLint and all harness tests."
  "2026-10-23T21:58:57.533Z",codex-agent,"Final local evidence: six pm-linked commands passed (29 executions, 28 distinct tests). Behavioral revert of only filename hashing compiled and failed the unique-digest assertion, then exact source restoration passed. Full just release-check with isolated Git configuration reached 514 passed tests and one five-second native-child deadline failure; isolated cargo +1.90.0 test --locked --test orientation_differential relationship_large_edge_limit_finishes_at_budget_floor -- --exact also hit that deadline on a later query (68.65 seconds total). This is the existing pm-rust-local-packet-deadline condition; only exact-head CI can complete the full gate evidence. Standalone just crash-check passed TypeScript, ESLint and 22 of 22 tests, including real non-git syscall crash/restart and update/comment first-fsync recovery. Main remains the reviewed PR 105 merge, and remote PR 110 head has not moved. Conflict resolution retains both Bun setup and Linux strace installation. Changelog regeneration is byte-identical; regenerate once more after these final tracker writes and require its check. Implementation work is complete; keep this item in progress and release the claim for independent verification. No threads replied to or resolved; no release or PR merge."
  "2026-10-23T22:02:40.831Z",codex-agent,"CI on merge 508bd7b exposed a test portability error: macOS rejects the invalid-UTF-8 filesystem rename with Illegal byte sequence. Correct the regression fixture, retaining a Linux real-session filesystem test and adding a Unix Admission::copy digest test using valid source and target files with distinct raw relative-name bytes. This verifies the exact hashing boundary on macOS without assuming its filesystem admits such names. Production hashing and all release thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-23T22:07:47.748Z",codex-agent,"Portable regression verification: cargo +1.90.0 test --locked --lib snapshot_digest_preserves_non_utf8 passed both cases. Restoring only Admission::copy to lossy relative.to_string_lossy().as_bytes() compiled and made BOTH the real Linux filename/directory session test and the Unix raw-relative-name digest test fail their unique-digest assertions (0 passed, 2 failed, exit 101). Exact production source restored. All seven pm-linked commands then passed: 19 session units, 7 CLI/SDK contracts, three supporting single cases, one original digest rerun and two prefix-filtered digest reruns (32 executions, 29 distinct tests). Strict all-target/all-feature Clippy and formatting passed. Initial CI run 40030616438 failed macOS only on the invalid-filename fixture; the correction retains real-filesystem coverage on Linux and validates the same exact digest boundary on Unix with ordinary source and target files. Final CI must rerun all four unchanged aggregate gates. The local five-second packet deadline remains covered by pm-rust-local-packet-deadline; no unrelated production changes or threshold changes."
